**Constant-time code** avoids branches or memory access patterns that depend on secret data, so timing can't leak them. Crypto libraries write it deliberately.

```text
// leaky: time and cache footprint depend on `secretByte`
if (table[secretByte] == target) { ... }

// constant-time: touches all entries, same pattern every time
for (i = 0; i < 256; i++) {
    result |= mask(i == secretByte) & table[i];
}
```

Slower, but the pattern never gives the secret away.
